{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The Gemini Developer API has no regional endpoint. If you need EU data residency, CMEK, or VPC-SC, you have to run Gemini on Vertex AI."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-vertex"},{"type":"text","value":" is that path. It builds the existing Gemini adapters with Vertex auth. Request mapping, tools, and streaming stay the same."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Claude on Vertex is a different package. See "},{"type":"link","href":"./anthropic#claude-on-vertex","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Anthropic Vertex"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"installation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Installation"}]},{"type":"component","name":"tabs","attributes":{"variant":"package-manager","mode":"install"},"children":[],"properties":{"data-package-manager-meta":"{\"packagesByFramework\":{\"react\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-vertex\"]],\"vue\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-vertex\"]],\"solid\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-vertex\"]],\"svelte\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-vertex\"]],\"preact\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-vertex\"]],\"angular\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-vertex\"]],\"vanilla\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-vertex\"]],\"octane\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-vertex\"]]},\"mode\":\"install\"}"}},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"basic-usage","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Basic usage"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { chat } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { vertexText } from \"@tanstack/ai-vertex\";\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: vertexText(\"gemini-3.7-flash\", {\n    project: \"my-project\",\n    location: \"europe-west1\",\n  }),\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"Hello!\" }],\n});","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Reuse one auth object for every factory:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { vertexImage, vertexText } from \"@tanstack/ai-vertex\";\n\nconst auth = {\n  project: \"my-project\",\n  location: \"europe-west1\",\n};\n\nconst text = vertexText(\"gemini-3.7-flash\", auth);\nconst image = vertexImage(\"gemini-3.1-flash-image\", auth);","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"authentication","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Authentication"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Vertex factories accept every auth option "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@google/genai"},{"type":"text","value":" accepts. They do "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"not"}]},{"type":"text","value":" read "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"GEMINI_API_KEY"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"GOOGLE_API_KEY"},{"type":"text","value":". Those keys are AI Studio, not Vertex."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"application-default-credentials","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Application Default Credentials"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This is the usual Google Cloud path. Sign in with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gcloud auth application-default login"},{"type":"text","value":", or set "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS"},{"type":"text","value":" to a service account JSON file."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pass "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"project"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"location"},{"type":"text","value":" on the factory, or set:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"GOOGLE_CLOUD_PROJECT=my-project\nGOOGLE_CLOUD_LOCATION=europe-west1","lang":"bash"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"GOOGLE_VERTEX_PROJECT"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"GOOGLE_VERTEX_LOCATION"},{"type":"text","value":" are also accepted."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { vertexText } from \"@tanstack/ai-vertex\";\n\nconst adapter = vertexText(\"gemini-3.7-flash\", {\n  project: \"my-project\",\n  location: \"europe-west1\",\n});","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"service-account-fields","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Service account fields"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { vertexText } from \"@tanstack/ai-vertex\";\n\nconst adapter = vertexText(\"gemini-3.7-flash\", {\n  project: \"my-project\",\n  location: \"europe-west1\",\n  googleAuthOptions: {\n    credentials: {\n      client_email: \"sa@my-project.iam.gserviceaccount.com\",\n      private_key: \"-----BEGIN PRIVATE KEY-----\\n...\\n-----END PRIVATE KEY-----\\n\",\n    },\n  },\n});","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"express-api-key","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Express API key"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Vertex express mode uses an API key and does not need project or location."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { vertexText } from \"@tanstack/ai-vertex\";\n\nconst adapter = vertexText(\"gemini-3.7-flash\", {\n  apiKey: \"vertex-express-key\",\n});","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Or set "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"GOOGLE_VERTEX_API_KEY"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"example-server-and-client","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example: server and client"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Keep Vertex credentials on the server. The browser only talks to your route."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Server:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { chat, toServerSentEventsResponse } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { vertexText } from \"@tanstack/ai-vertex\";\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const { messages } = await request.json();\n\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: vertexText(\"gemini-3.7-flash\", {\n      project: \"my-project\",\n      location: \"europe-west1\",\n    }),\n    messages,\n  });\n\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream);\n}","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Client:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { useChat, fetchServerSentEvents } from \"@tanstack/ai-react\";\n\nexport function Chat() {\n  const { messages, sendMessage } = useChat({\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents(\"/api/chat\"),\n  });\n\n  return (\n    <form\n      onSubmit={(event) => {\n        event.preventDefault();\n        const form = event.currentTarget;\n        const input = new FormData(form).get(\"text\");\n        if (typeof input === \"string\" && input.trim()) {\n          sendMessage(input);\n          form.reset();\n        }\n      }}\n    >\n      {messages.map((message) => (\n        <div key={message.id}>\n          {message.role}:{\" \"}\n          {message.parts\n            .filter((part) => part.type === \"text\")\n            .map((part) => part.content)\n            .join(\"\")}\n        </div>\n      ))}\n      <input name=\"text\" />\n      <button type=\"submit\">Send</button>\n    </form>\n  );\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useChat"},{"type":"text","value":" does not know this is Vertex. It only consumes the SSE stream from your server."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"other-gemini-activities","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Other Gemini activities"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Every factory uses the same auth object."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import {\n  vertexAudio,\n  vertexEmbedding,\n  vertexImage,\n  vertexSpeech,\n  vertexSummarize,\n  vertexText,\n  vertexVideo,\n} from \"@tanstack/ai-vertex\";\n\nconst auth = { project: \"my-project\", location: \"europe-west1\" };\n\nvertexText(\"gemini-3.7-flash\", auth);\nvertexSummarize(\"gemini-3.7-flash\", auth);\nvertexImage(\"gemini-3.1-flash-image\", auth);\nvertexEmbedding(\"gemini-embedding-001\", auth);\nvertexSpeech(\"gemini-3.1-flash-tts-preview\", auth);\nvertexAudio(\"lyria-3-pro-preview\", auth);\nvertexVideo(\"veo-3.1-generate-preview\", auth);","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Model ids and provider options are the same as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-gemini"},{"type":"text","value":". Vertex-only image options (for example "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"9:21"},{"type":"text","value":") are not unlocked in this release."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"environment-variables","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Environment variables"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Variable"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Purpose"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"GOOGLE_CLOUD_PROJECT"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"GCP project id"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"GOOGLE_VERTEX_PROJECT"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Alias for the project id"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"GOOGLE_CLOUD_LOCATION"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Region, for example "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"europe-west1"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"GOOGLE_VERTEX_LOCATION"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Alias for the region"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"GOOGLE_VERTEX_API_KEY"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Vertex express API key"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Path to a service account JSON file"}]}]]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"api-reference","children":[{"type":"text","value":"API reference"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"vertextext-model-config","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"vertexText(model, config?)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Creates a Gemini chat adapter on Vertex."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"vertexsummarize-model-config","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"vertexSummarize(model, config?)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Creates a Gemini summarize adapter on Vertex."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"verteximage-model-config","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"vertexImage(model, config?)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Creates a Gemini image adapter on Vertex."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"vertexembedding-model-config","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"vertexEmbedding(model, config?)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Creates a Gemini embedding adapter on Vertex."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"vertexspeech-model-config","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"vertexSpeech(model, config?)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Creates a Gemini text-to-speech adapter on Vertex. Experimental."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"vertexaudio-model-config","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"vertexAudio(model, config?)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Creates a Gemini Lyria audio adapter on Vertex. Experimental."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"vertexvideo-model-config","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"vertexVideo(model, config?)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Creates a Gemini video adapter on Vertex. Experimental. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"config.allowUrlFetch"},{"type":"text","value":" is the same opt-in as the Gemini video adapter."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"config"},{"type":"text","value":" accepts "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"project"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"location"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"apiKey"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"googleAuthOptions"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"httpOptions"},{"type":"text","value":", and the other "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@google/genai"},{"type":"text","value":" client fields. The factory always sets "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"vertexai: true"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"claude-on-vertex","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Claude on Vertex"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use "},{"type":"link","href":"./anthropic#claude-on-vertex","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"anthropicVertexText"}]},{"type":"text","value":" from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-anthropic/vertex"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"grok-on-vertex","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Grok on Vertex"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use "},{"type":"link","href":"./grok#grok-on-vertex","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"grokVertexText"}]},{"type":"text","value":" from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-grok/vertex"},{"type":"text","value":". Vertex Grok uses the OpenAI-compatible Responses endpoint. Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"grokVertexSummarize"},{"type":"text","value":" from the same entry for summarize. The factory accepts only the Grok chat models in the Vertex catalog ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"grok-4.3"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"grok-4.20-reasoning"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"grok-4.20-non-reasoning"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"grok-4.1-fast-reasoning"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"grok-4.1-fast-non-reasoning"},{"type":"text","value":")."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"mistral-on-vertex","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Mistral on Vertex"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use "},{"type":"link","href":"./mistral#mistral-on-vertex","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"mistralVertexText"}]},{"type":"text","value":" from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-mistral/vertex"},{"type":"text","value":". Vertex Mistral uses the publisher "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"rawPredict"},{"type":"text","value":" path. It is regional only ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"us-central1"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"europe-west4"},{"type":"text","value":"). The factory accepts only the Mistral chat models in the Vertex catalog ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"mistral-medium-3"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"mistral-small-2503"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"codestral-2"},{"type":"text","value":")."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"installation","text":"Installation","level":2},{"id":"basic-usage","text":"Basic usage","level":2},{"id":"authentication","text":"Authentication","level":2},{"id":"application-default-credentials","text":"Application Default Credentials","level":3},{"id":"service-account-fields","text":"Service account fields","level":3},{"id":"express-api-key","text":"Express API key","level":3},{"id":"example-server-and-client","text":"Example: server and client","level":2},{"id":"other-gemini-activities","text":"Other Gemini activities","level":2},{"id":"environment-variables","text":"Environment variables","level":2},{"id":"api-reference","text":"API reference","level":2},{"id":"vertextext-model-config","text":"vertexText(model, config?)","level":3},{"id":"vertexsummarize-model-config","text":"vertexSummarize(model, config?)","level":3},{"id":"verteximage-model-config","text":"vertexImage(model, config?)","level":3},{"id":"vertexembedding-model-config","text":"vertexEmbedding(model, config?)","level":3},{"id":"vertexspeech-model-config","text":"vertexSpeech(model, config?)","level":3},{"id":"vertexaudio-model-config","text":"vertexAudio(model, config?)","level":3},{"id":"vertexvideo-model-config","text":"vertexVideo(model, config?)","level":3},{"id":"claude-on-vertex","text":"Claude on Vertex","level":2},{"id":"grok-on-vertex","text":"Grok on Vertex","level":2},{"id":"mistral-on-vertex","text":"Mistral on Vertex","level":2}]},"frameworks":["react","vue","solid","svelte","preact","angular","vanilla","octane"],"downloadMarkdown":"\nThe Gemini Developer API has no regional endpoint. If you need EU data residency, CMEK, or VPC-SC, you have to run Gemini on Vertex AI.\n\n`@tanstack/ai-vertex` is that path. It builds the existing Gemini adapters with Vertex auth. Request mapping, tools, and streaming stay the same.\n\nClaude on Vertex is a different package. See [Anthropic Vertex](./anthropic#claude-on-vertex).\n\n## Installation\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"install\" -->\n\nreact: @tanstack/ai-vertex\nvue: @tanstack/ai-vertex\nsolid: @tanstack/ai-vertex\nsvelte: @tanstack/ai-vertex\npreact: @tanstack/ai-vertex\nangular: @tanstack/ai-vertex\nvanilla: @tanstack/ai-vertex\noctane: @tanstack/ai-vertex\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\n## Basic usage\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { vertexText } from \"@tanstack/ai-vertex\";\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: vertexText(\"gemini-3.7-flash\", {\n    project: \"my-project\",\n    location: \"europe-west1\",\n  }),\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"Hello!\" }],\n});\n```\n\nReuse one auth object for every factory:\n\n```typescript\nimport { vertexImage, vertexText } from \"@tanstack/ai-vertex\";\n\nconst auth = {\n  project: \"my-project\",\n  location: \"europe-west1\",\n};\n\nconst text = vertexText(\"gemini-3.7-flash\", auth);\nconst image = vertexImage(\"gemini-3.1-flash-image\", auth);\n```\n\n## Authentication\n\nVertex factories accept every auth option `@google/genai` accepts. They do **not** read `GEMINI_API_KEY` or `GOOGLE_API_KEY`. Those keys are AI Studio, not Vertex.\n\n### Application Default Credentials\n\nThis is the usual Google Cloud path. Sign in with `gcloud auth application-default login`, or set `GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS` to a service account JSON file.\n\nPass `project` and `location` on the factory, or set:\n\n```bash\nGOOGLE_CLOUD_PROJECT=my-project\nGOOGLE_CLOUD_LOCATION=europe-west1\n```\n\n`GOOGLE_VERTEX_PROJECT` and `GOOGLE_VERTEX_LOCATION` are also accepted.\n\n```typescript\nimport { vertexText } from \"@tanstack/ai-vertex\";\n\nconst adapter = vertexText(\"gemini-3.7-flash\", {\n  project: \"my-project\",\n  location: \"europe-west1\",\n});\n```\n\n### Service account fields\n\n```typescript\nimport { vertexText } from \"@tanstack/ai-vertex\";\n\nconst adapter = vertexText(\"gemini-3.7-flash\", {\n  project: \"my-project\",\n  location: \"europe-west1\",\n  googleAuthOptions: {\n    credentials: {\n      client_email: \"sa@my-project.iam.gserviceaccount.com\",\n      private_key: \"-----BEGIN PRIVATE KEY-----\\n...\\n-----END PRIVATE KEY-----\\n\",\n    },\n  },\n});\n```\n\n### Express API key\n\nVertex express mode uses an API key and does not need project or location.\n\n```typescript\nimport { vertexText } from \"@tanstack/ai-vertex\";\n\nconst adapter = vertexText(\"gemini-3.7-flash\", {\n  apiKey: \"vertex-express-key\",\n});\n```\n\nOr set `GOOGLE_VERTEX_API_KEY`.\n\n## Example: server and client\n\nKeep Vertex credentials on the server. The browser only talks to your route.\n\nServer:\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat, toServerSentEventsResponse } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { vertexText } from \"@tanstack/ai-vertex\";\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const { messages } = await request.json();\n\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: vertexText(\"gemini-3.7-flash\", {\n      project: \"my-project\",\n      location: \"europe-west1\",\n    }),\n    messages,\n  });\n\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream);\n}\n```\n\nClient:\n\n```tsx\nimport { useChat, fetchServerSentEvents } from \"@tanstack/ai-react\";\n\nexport function Chat() {\n  const { messages, sendMessage } = useChat({\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents(\"/api/chat\"),\n  });\n\n  return (\n    <form\n      onSubmit={(event) => {\n        event.preventDefault();\n        const form = event.currentTarget;\n        const input = new FormData(form).get(\"text\");\n        if (typeof input === \"string\" && input.trim()) {\n          sendMessage(input);\n          form.reset();\n        }\n      }}\n    >\n      {messages.map((message) => (\n        <div key={message.id}>\n          {message.role}:{\" \"}\n          {message.parts\n            .filter((part) => part.type === \"text\")\n            .map((part) => part.content)\n            .join(\"\")}\n        </div>\n      ))}\n      <input name=\"text\" />\n      <button type=\"submit\">Send</button>\n    </form>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n`useChat` does not know this is Vertex. It only consumes the SSE stream from your server.\n\n## Other Gemini activities\n\nEvery factory uses the same auth object.\n\n```typescript\nimport {\n  vertexAudio,\n  vertexEmbedding,\n  vertexImage,\n  vertexSpeech,\n  vertexSummarize,\n  vertexText,\n  vertexVideo,\n} from \"@tanstack/ai-vertex\";\n\nconst auth = { project: \"my-project\", location: \"europe-west1\" };\n\nvertexText(\"gemini-3.7-flash\", auth);\nvertexSummarize(\"gemini-3.7-flash\", auth);\nvertexImage(\"gemini-3.1-flash-image\", auth);\nvertexEmbedding(\"gemini-embedding-001\", auth);\nvertexSpeech(\"gemini-3.1-flash-tts-preview\", auth);\nvertexAudio(\"lyria-3-pro-preview\", auth);\nvertexVideo(\"veo-3.1-generate-preview\", auth);\n```\n\nModel ids and provider options are the same as `@tanstack/ai-gemini`. Vertex-only image options (for example `9:21`) are not unlocked in this release.\n\n## Environment variables\n\n| Variable | Purpose |\n| --- | --- |\n| `GOOGLE_CLOUD_PROJECT` | GCP project id |\n| `GOOGLE_VERTEX_PROJECT` | Alias for the project id |\n| `GOOGLE_CLOUD_LOCATION` | Region, for example `europe-west1` |\n| `GOOGLE_VERTEX_LOCATION` | Alias for the region |\n| `GOOGLE_VERTEX_API_KEY` | Vertex express API key |\n| `GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS` | Path to a service account JSON file |\n\n## API reference\n\n### `vertexText(model, config?)`\n\nCreates a Gemini chat adapter on Vertex.\n\n### `vertexSummarize(model, config?)`\n\nCreates a Gemini summarize adapter on Vertex.\n\n### `vertexImage(model, config?)`\n\nCreates a Gemini image adapter on Vertex.\n\n### `vertexEmbedding(model, config?)`\n\nCreates a Gemini embedding adapter on Vertex.\n\n### `vertexSpeech(model, config?)`\n\nCreates a Gemini text-to-speech adapter on Vertex. Experimental.\n\n### `vertexAudio(model, config?)`\n\nCreates a Gemini Lyria audio adapter on Vertex. Experimental.\n\n### `vertexVideo(model, config?)`\n\nCreates a Gemini video adapter on Vertex. Experimental. `config.allowUrlFetch` is the same opt-in as the Gemini video adapter.\n\n`config` accepts `project`, `location`, `apiKey`, `googleAuthOptions`, `httpOptions`, and the other `@google/genai` client fields. The factory always sets `vertexai: true`.\n\n## Claude on Vertex\n\nUse [`anthropicVertexText`](./anthropic#claude-on-vertex) from `@tanstack/ai-anthropic/vertex`.\n\n## Grok on Vertex\n\nUse [`grokVertexText`](./grok#grok-on-vertex) from `@tanstack/ai-grok/vertex`. Vertex Grok uses the OpenAI-compatible Responses endpoint. Use `grokVertexSummarize` from the same entry for summarize. The factory accepts only the Grok chat models in the Vertex catalog (`grok-4.3`, `grok-4.20-reasoning`, `grok-4.20-non-reasoning`, `grok-4.1-fast-reasoning`, `grok-4.1-fast-non-reasoning`).\n\n## Mistral on Vertex\n\nUse [`mistralVertexText`](./mistral#mistral-on-vertex) from `@tanstack/ai-mistral/vertex`. Vertex Mistral uses the publisher `rawPredict` path. It is regional only (`us-central1` or `europe-west4`). The factory accepts only the Mistral chat models in the Vertex catalog (`mistral-medium-3`, `mistral-small-2503`, `codestral-2`).\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Google Vertex AI\nid: vertex-adapter\norder: 4\ndescription: \"Run Gemini on Google Vertex AI with TanStack AI. Use regional endpoints and Google Cloud credentials via @tanstack/ai-vertex.\"\nkeywords:\n  - tanstack ai\n  - vertex\n  - vertex ai\n  - gemini\n  - grok\n  - xai\n  - mistral\n  - google cloud\n  - regional\n  - adapter\n---\n\nThe Gemini Developer API has no regional endpoint. If you need EU data residency, CMEK, or VPC-SC, you have to run Gemini on Vertex AI.\n\n`@tanstack/ai-vertex` is that path. It builds the existing Gemini adapters with Vertex auth. Request mapping, tools, and streaming stay the same.\n\nClaude on Vertex is a different package. See [Anthropic Vertex](./anthropic#claude-on-vertex).\n\n## Installation\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"install\" -->\n\nreact: @tanstack/ai-vertex\nvue: @tanstack/ai-vertex\nsolid: @tanstack/ai-vertex\nsvelte: @tanstack/ai-vertex\npreact: @tanstack/ai-vertex\nangular: @tanstack/ai-vertex\nvanilla: @tanstack/ai-vertex\noctane: @tanstack/ai-vertex\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\n## Basic usage\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { vertexText } from \"@tanstack/ai-vertex\";\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: vertexText(\"gemini-3.7-flash\", {\n    project: \"my-project\",\n    location: \"europe-west1\",\n  }),\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"Hello!\" }],\n});\n```\n\nReuse one auth object for every factory:\n\n```typescript\nimport { vertexImage, vertexText } from \"@tanstack/ai-vertex\";\n\nconst auth = {\n  project: \"my-project\",\n  location: \"europe-west1\",\n};\n\nconst text = vertexText(\"gemini-3.7-flash\", auth);\nconst image = vertexImage(\"gemini-3.1-flash-image\", auth);\n```\n\n## Authentication\n\nVertex factories accept every auth option `@google/genai` accepts. They do **not** read `GEMINI_API_KEY` or `GOOGLE_API_KEY`. Those keys are AI Studio, not Vertex.\n\n### Application Default Credentials\n\nThis is the usual Google Cloud path. Sign in with `gcloud auth application-default login`, or set `GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS` to a service account JSON file.\n\nPass `project` and `location` on the factory, or set:\n\n```bash\nGOOGLE_CLOUD_PROJECT=my-project\nGOOGLE_CLOUD_LOCATION=europe-west1\n```\n\n`GOOGLE_VERTEX_PROJECT` and `GOOGLE_VERTEX_LOCATION` are also accepted.\n\n```typescript\nimport { vertexText } from \"@tanstack/ai-vertex\";\n\nconst adapter = vertexText(\"gemini-3.7-flash\", {\n  project: \"my-project\",\n  location: \"europe-west1\",\n});\n```\n\n### Service account fields\n\n```typescript\nimport { vertexText } from \"@tanstack/ai-vertex\";\n\nconst adapter = vertexText(\"gemini-3.7-flash\", {\n  project: \"my-project\",\n  location: \"europe-west1\",\n  googleAuthOptions: {\n    credentials: {\n      client_email: \"sa@my-project.iam.gserviceaccount.com\",\n      private_key: \"-----BEGIN PRIVATE KEY-----\\n...\\n-----END PRIVATE KEY-----\\n\",\n    },\n  },\n});\n```\n\n### Express API key\n\nVertex express mode uses an API key and does not need project or location.\n\n```typescript\nimport { vertexText } from \"@tanstack/ai-vertex\";\n\nconst adapter = vertexText(\"gemini-3.7-flash\", {\n  apiKey: \"vertex-express-key\",\n});\n```\n\nOr set `GOOGLE_VERTEX_API_KEY`.\n\n## Example: server and client\n\nKeep Vertex credentials on the server. The browser only talks to your route.\n\nServer:\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat, toServerSentEventsResponse } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { vertexText } from \"@tanstack/ai-vertex\";\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const { messages } = await request.json();\n\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: vertexText(\"gemini-3.7-flash\", {\n      project: \"my-project\",\n      location: \"europe-west1\",\n    }),\n    messages,\n  });\n\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream);\n}\n```\n\nClient:\n\n```tsx\nimport { useChat, fetchServerSentEvents } from \"@tanstack/ai-react\";\n\nexport function Chat() {\n  const { messages, sendMessage } = useChat({\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents(\"/api/chat\"),\n  });\n\n  return (\n    <form\n      onSubmit={(event) => {\n        event.preventDefault();\n        const form = event.currentTarget;\n        const input = new FormData(form).get(\"text\");\n        if (typeof input === \"string\" && input.trim()) {\n          sendMessage(input);\n          form.reset();\n        }\n      }}\n    >\n      {messages.map((message) => (\n        <div key={message.id}>\n          {message.role}:{\" \"}\n          {message.parts\n            .filter((part) => part.type === \"text\")\n            .map((part) => part.content)\n            .join(\"\")}\n        </div>\n      ))}\n      <input name=\"text\" />\n      <button type=\"submit\">Send</button>\n    </form>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n`useChat` does not know this is Vertex. It only consumes the SSE stream from your server.\n\n## Other Gemini activities\n\nEvery factory uses the same auth object.\n\n```typescript\nimport {\n  vertexAudio,\n  vertexEmbedding,\n  vertexImage,\n  vertexSpeech,\n  vertexSummarize,\n  vertexText,\n  vertexVideo,\n} from \"@tanstack/ai-vertex\";\n\nconst auth = { project: \"my-project\", location: \"europe-west1\" };\n\nvertexText(\"gemini-3.7-flash\", auth);\nvertexSummarize(\"gemini-3.7-flash\", auth);\nvertexImage(\"gemini-3.1-flash-image\", auth);\nvertexEmbedding(\"gemini-embedding-001\", auth);\nvertexSpeech(\"gemini-3.1-flash-tts-preview\", auth);\nvertexAudio(\"lyria-3-pro-preview\", auth);\nvertexVideo(\"veo-3.1-generate-preview\", auth);\n```\n\nModel ids and provider options are the same as `@tanstack/ai-gemini`. Vertex-only image options (for example `9:21`) are not unlocked in this release.\n\n## Environment variables\n\n| Variable | Purpose |\n| --- | --- |\n| `GOOGLE_CLOUD_PROJECT` | GCP project id |\n| `GOOGLE_VERTEX_PROJECT` | Alias for the project id |\n| `GOOGLE_CLOUD_LOCATION` | Region, for example `europe-west1` |\n| `GOOGLE_VERTEX_LOCATION` | Alias for the region |\n| `GOOGLE_VERTEX_API_KEY` | Vertex express API key |\n| `GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS` | Path to a service account JSON file |\n\n## API reference\n\n### `vertexText(model, config?)`\n\nCreates a Gemini chat adapter on Vertex.\n\n### `vertexSummarize(model, config?)`\n\nCreates a Gemini summarize adapter on Vertex.\n\n### `vertexImage(model, config?)`\n\nCreates a Gemini image adapter on Vertex.\n\n### `vertexEmbedding(model, config?)`\n\nCreates a Gemini embedding adapter on Vertex.\n\n### `vertexSpeech(model, config?)`\n\nCreates a Gemini text-to-speech adapter on Vertex. Experimental.\n\n### `vertexAudio(model, config?)`\n\nCreates a Gemini Lyria audio adapter on Vertex. Experimental.\n\n### `vertexVideo(model, config?)`\n\nCreates a Gemini video adapter on Vertex. Experimental. `config.allowUrlFetch` is the same opt-in as the Gemini video adapter.\n\n`config` accepts `project`, `location`, `apiKey`, `googleAuthOptions`, `httpOptions`, and the other `@google/genai` client fields. The factory always sets `vertexai: true`.\n\n## Claude on Vertex\n\nUse [`anthropicVertexText`](./anthropic#claude-on-vertex) from `@tanstack/ai-anthropic/vertex`.\n\n## Grok on Vertex\n\nUse [`grokVertexText`](./grok#grok-on-vertex) from `@tanstack/ai-grok/vertex`. Vertex Grok uses the OpenAI-compatible Responses endpoint. Use `grokVertexSummarize` from the same entry for summarize. The factory accepts only the Grok chat models in the Vertex catalog (`grok-4.3`, `grok-4.20-reasoning`, `grok-4.20-non-reasoning`, `grok-4.1-fast-reasoning`, `grok-4.1-fast-non-reasoning`).\n\n## Mistral on Vertex\n\nUse [`mistralVertexText`](./mistral#mistral-on-vertex) from `@tanstack/ai-mistral/vertex`. Vertex Mistral uses the publisher `rawPredict` path. It is regional only (`us-central1` or `europe-west4`). The factory accepts only the Mistral chat models in the Vertex catalog (`mistral-medium-3`, `mistral-small-2503`, `codestral-2`).\n"}
